    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n43212" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἑτερό-στομος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>one-edged</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πέλεκυς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Poll.
					1.137
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἑ. φάλαγξ</span> a marching formation in
			which the <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λοχαγοί</span> of the leading
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κέρας</span> are on the r., those of
			the rear <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κέρας</span> on the l., or vice
			versa, <i><span class="en">
				Ascl.
				<u>Tact.</u>
				10.22
			</span></i>, etc. Adv. -<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μως</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				11.4
			</span></i>.</div>
